      "id": 1,
      "text": "Stamford was laid out in 1887 when the Chicago, Burlington and Quincy Railroad extended to that point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stamford%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Stamford was likely named after Stamford, Connecticut, which itself takes its name from Stamford, Lincolnshire, England.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stamford%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Belgian settlers established farms south of Stamford, attracted by CB&Q’s promotional campaigns offering reduced passenger rates and land grants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
